{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Get you up from among this congregation</b> – I do not understand the reason of this verse and its companion above, \"Separate yourselves from among this congregation\" (Numbers 16:21), for it is within the power of Elohim to slay many by plague around a single righteous man while he alone survives, as happened with the firstborn of Egypt. And so it was in all the plagues — three sleeping in one cloak, the two die and the one in the middle escapes. It appears that the wrath was going forth to slay the entire congregation just as the wicked ones who followed them perished by the opening of the mouth of the earth or by the fire that went forth, and these are comprehensive blows suited to slay all who stand there together, unless a second miracle were performed for those who escape, or the Holy One, blessed be He, said thus for the honor of the righteous, that as long as they are among them He would not send His hand against them. And the intention in these and similar cases is to make known that they need supplication for mercy and atonement, and Moses is the one who urges to do so immediately:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The phrase 'three sleeping in one cloak' (שלשה ישנים בטלית אחת) refers to the well-known midrashic motif of divine selectivity in plague; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:34.004875704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}